{{!-- Advantage / Normal / Disadvantage, as a segmented pill.

      Its own partial rather than markup inline in the moves tab so the character sheet's
      sidebar copy can adopt the same shape later without the two being retyped. Only the
      steading uses it today; the character sheet still carries the stacked radio list, which
      is what suits its narrow sidebar.

      It rides in a section HEADING (see steading-tab-moves.hbs), the same place and the same
      component as the Relationships card's table/board toggle two tabs over. That is the
      point: this used to be a section of its own, with a page-wide underline and the visual
      weight of the page's actual subject, for a three-way toggle.

      `stonetop-section-heading-control` is what makes folding the section fold the pill with
      it (see `_wireSectionCollapse`) — a roll modifier over hidden moves is a dead end.

      Buttons, not the radio inputs a segmented picker normally pairs with: a NAMED input
      inside an actor sheet's form is submitted into `_updateObject` and lands in
      `expandObject(formData)` as a stray top-level key. Same reason the relationships view
      toggle is buttons. `is-active` is server-stamped, which is safe because the flip always
      re-renders.

      Worst to best, left to right — Disadvantage, Normal, Advantage — so the strip reads as a
      scale rather than a menu.

      DRAWN ONLY WHEN THE MODE IS NOT ASKED PER ROLL. The "Ask How to Roll Each Time" client
      setting moves the choice into the pre-roll window (module/dialogs/RollDialog.js), which
      starts at Normal every time; a sticky control beside it would be a second answer to the
      same question, and the window would win. The mount points test the setting, not this file —
      a partial that renders nothing would still leave its section heading behind.

      Params: rollMode ("adv" | "normal" | "dis"). --}}
<div class="stonetop-roll-mode-bar stonetop-section-heading-control">
	<div class="stonetop-segmented-picker stonetop-roll-mode-picker" role="group"
	     aria-label="{{localize "stonetop.rollMode.label"}}">
		<button type="button"
		        class="stonetop-segmented-picker-option stonetop-roll-mode-btn{{#if (eq rollMode "dis")}} is-active{{/if}}"
		        data-roll-mode="dis"
		        aria-pressed="{{#if (eq rollMode "dis")}}true{{else}}false{{/if}}"
		        data-tooltip="{{localize "stonetop.rollMode.disTooltip"}}">
			<i class="fa-solid fa-angles-down" aria-hidden="true"></i>
			<span>{{localize "stonetop.rollMode.dis"}}</span>
		</button>
		<button type="button"
		        class="stonetop-segmented-picker-option stonetop-roll-mode-btn{{#if (eq rollMode "normal")}} is-active{{/if}}"
		        data-roll-mode="normal"
		        aria-pressed="{{#if (eq rollMode "normal")}}true{{else}}false{{/if}}"
		        data-tooltip="{{localize "stonetop.rollMode.normalTooltip"}}">
			<i class="fa-solid fa-equals" aria-hidden="true"></i>
			<span>{{localize "stonetop.rollMode.normal"}}</span>
		</button>
		<button type="button"
		        class="stonetop-segmented-picker-option stonetop-roll-mode-btn{{#if (eq rollMode "adv")}} is-active{{/if}}"
		        data-roll-mode="adv"
		        aria-pressed="{{#if (eq rollMode "adv")}}true{{else}}false{{/if}}"
		        data-tooltip="{{localize "stonetop.rollMode.advTooltip"}}">
			<i class="fa-solid fa-angles-up" aria-hidden="true"></i>
			<span>{{localize "stonetop.rollMode.adv"}}</span>
		</button>
	</div>
</div>
